@bank all
// Pillar 5 (head writer, seat W): the fault tables' words (plans/mechanics/fault-tables.html), for section 17's
// FAULT_CAUSES (seat S), the scanner (H) and head-scratchers (H). TEXTS. Keys: fault.<what>.<kind>.<cause>.
// name: the cause in plain words. shows: the job card's symptom. sign: what you see up close. still: the machine's
// line when you FIT this cause's part and it wasn't the problem (never names the real cause). tried: a crew note
// in a head-scratcher when someone fitted this cause's part (the game adds the name). Settings and loads have no
// part, so no still or tried. Cause ids (proposed; tell the writer if S's differ): the part's short name, 'drift' for
// a setting, 'junction' for the galley load.

// oven · element
== fault.name.oven.element
- The element is failing
== fault.shows.oven.element
- runs cool
== fault.sign.oven.element
- Cool all over, slow to heat.
== fault.still.oven.element
- Fitted a new element. It still runs cool.
== fault.tried.oven.element
- New element in. Still runs cool.

// oven · seal
== fault.name.oven.seal
- The door seal is worn
== fault.shows.oven.seal
- runs cool
== fault.sign.oven.seal
- Cool by the door. You feel heat at the gap.
== fault.still.oven.seal
- New door seal in. No change: it still runs cool.
== fault.tried.oven.seal
- Swapped the door seal. Still runs cool.

// oven · belt
== fault.name.oven.belt
- The fan's belt is slipping
== fault.shows.oven.belt
- runs cool
== fault.sign.oven.belt
- Hot at the back, cool at the front. A squeal at start.
== fault.still.oven.belt
- Fitted a new fan belt. It still runs cool.
== fault.tried.oven.belt
- Fitted a fresh fan belt. Still runs cool.

// oven · drift
== fault.name.oven.drift
- Its setting has drifted
== fault.shows.oven.drift
- runs hot
== fault.sign.oven.drift
- The glow stutters.

// oven · junction
== fault.name.oven.junction
- The galley's power junction sags under load
== fault.shows.oven.junction
- runs cool
== fault.sign.oven.junction
- Fine at breakfast, cool at dinner.

// range · element
== fault.name.range.element
- A ring's element is failing
== fault.shows.range.element
- a ring is weak
== fault.sign.range.element
- One ring slow, the others fine.
== fault.still.range.element
- New element in. No change: it still has a weak ring.
== fault.tried.range.element
- Fitted a fresh element. Still has a weak ring.

